      <marc:subfield code="a">For the first time as filmmaker, Chaplin stepped into feature-length storytelling with this tale of the down but never out Tramp (Chaplin) and the adorable ragamuffin (6-year-old Jackie Coogan) who, rescued as a foundling and raised in the School of Hard Knocks by the tramp, in his inseparable sidekick. Memorable scenes include a lesson in table manners, the bully brawl and the Tramp&apos;s angelic dream. The Kid earns its wings.</marc:subfield>
